---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Scale Readiness — Matthew Cochran"
  description="Scale Readiness Diagnostic: structured validation for Series A SaaS before you commit more headcount and budget."
>
  <Section heading="Scale Readiness" description="Structured validation before you scale">
    <div class="max-w-[65ch]">
    <p>I help Series A SaaS teams validate that they are truly ready to scale—across both how the system is built and how well it resonates with the market—before they commit more headcount and budget.</p>
    <p>This is not fractional CTO work, ongoing strategy workshops, or implementation. It is a <strong>time-bound diagnostic</strong> that produces decision-grade clarity: what will break when you scale, what must change first, and what to double down on or stop.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-text-headline)]">Scale Readiness Diagnostic (4–6 weeks)</h2>
    <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> You get clarity on structural and market risks before scaling decisions. No surprises after you hire.</p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold">Deliverables</h3>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6">
      <li><strong>Structural Scaling Map</strong> — Where coupling and boundary risk live; where hiring would amplify fragility; where normal changes spill across too many boundaries.</li>
      <li><strong>Market Resonance Risk Map</strong> — How clear your ideal customer is; gaps between features and that customer; roadmap and pre-sell signal gaps; where the funnel breaks down.</li>
      <li><strong>Scale Readiness Blueprint</strong> — What must change before scaling, what to kill, what to double down on, and how to sequence hiring and fixes.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold">What this is not</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
      <li>Staff augmentation or hands-on implementation.</li>
      <li>Ongoing refactoring or fractional CTO retainer.</li>
      <li>Strategy workshops without a concrete deliverable.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>It is a structured, time-bound validation. Engagements typically start at $25k+. I run a limited number at a time to keep depth and focus.</p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold">Who it's for</h3>
    <p>Series A SaaS, 10–50 engineers, hiring or planning to hire VP Eng / Head of Eng, with real scaling pressure and decision authority. Budget intent within 60 days.</p>
    <p>If that's not you yet, the diagnostic is not the right fit—but you can still take the <a href="/snapshot/">Scale Readiness Snapshot</a> to see where you stand.</p>

    <p>
      <a
        href="/snapshot/"
        class="mt-6 inline-block rounded border-2 border-[var(--color-primary)] px-6 py-3 text-[var(--color-text-emphasis)] no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-[var(--color-primary)]/10 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]"
      >
        Take the Scale Readiness Snapshot
      </a>
    </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
